  "query_preview": ".. \nIssued at 121 PM CDT Fri Jul 31 2026\n\nAn expansive mid-level ridge centered over the Desert Southwest will \nremain the dominant weather feature through early next week, \nmaintaining hot and predominately dry conditions across South Texas. \nA mid-level trough rounding the northeastern periphery of this ridge \nis expected to amplify over the Ohio Valley on Sunday, slightly \neroding the eastern edge of the aformentioned ridge. As a result, we \ncan expect increased mid-level moisture and small scale ascent \nacross the region. Even so, shower and thunderstorm chances will \nremain low, ranging from 15-20% on the high end, mainly across the \nCoastal Plains and Brush Country. \n\nA continuation of temperatures in the mid to upper 90's along the \ncoast and 100+ elsewhere is expected to hold into early next week. \nWhile widespread heat indicies will remain below 110 degrees, a \nmoderate to major (2 & 3) HeatRisk will remain in play the entire \nforecast period. These temperatures, coupled with gusty winds, have \nresulted in an increased fire risk for the western Brush Country. \nConditions may improve Sunday with a chance for rain over the \narea.",
